WEBVTT
NOTE OpenIE Research TV — rce-compile (90s) Narrator Lem

1
00:00:00.419 --> 00:00:06.252
Checked honestly against twelve production and verified compiler families,

2
00:00:06.252 --> 00:00:11.060
no single descriptive rule covers how compilers behave today.

3
00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:21.456
Static WebAssembly IR size predicts runtime energy poorly at R-squared 0.1154,

4
00:00:21.456 --> 00:00:27.540
whereas Regime-B execution profiling hits 0.9999.

5
00:00:28.251 --> 00:00:35.413
This three-dimensional prism traces source lowering through explicit equivalence levels,

6
00:00:35.413 --> 00:00:39.319
trusted-base digests, and nameless binary reuse.

7
00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:46.405
Every optimization tier from CPython and PyPy to Clang, GCC,

8
00:00:46.405 --> 00:00:52.886
and Rustc was checksum-verified on Linux Zen 5 RAPL counters.

9
00:00:53.597 --> 00:01:02.583
While aggressive O3 flags often lose energy on short-lived binaries,

10
00:01:02.583 --> 00:01:11.438
De Bruijn SHA-256 caching cuts Clang O3 167.8x and Rustc O3 448.5x.

11
00:01:12.149 --> 00:01:19.155
Five hundred execution-verified semantic mutants confirm De Bruijn safety,

12
00:01:19.155 --> 00:01:24.078
with Zen 5 RAPL figures strictly labeled reported_j.
